import re,os
N=[]
def n(cat,title,url,tools,diff,summ,steps,faqs,label): N.append((cat,title,url,tools,diff,summ,steps,faqs,label))
n("Show Control","Use QLab 5's OSC dictionary as an agent's control vocabulary","https://qlab.app/docs/v5/scripting/osc-dictionary-v5/",["QLab 5","OSC"],"Intermediate",
"Figure 53's official dictionary lists every OSC message QLab 5 accepts, so it's the reference an agent or script should use to target workspaces and cues.",
["Enable OSC access in QLab's workspace settings and set a passcode if you need one.","Use workspace-level messages like /go, /panic and /save, or address cues as /cue/{number}/{command}.","Paste the relevant dictionary sections into your agent's context or tool descriptions so it only sends documented messages.","Check each message's permissions (view, edit, control) before giving an agent write access."],
[("How do I target a specific workspace?","Use /workspace/{id}/..., where {id} is the workspace's display name (e.g. hamlet.qlab5) or its unique ID."),("Why give this to an agent?","Agents work better with an authoritative command list than guessing OSC paths.")],"Figure 53 QLab 5 documentation")
n("Show Control","Generate hundreds of sequential show control cues in QLab","https://qlab.app/cookbook/show-control-cues-generator/",["QLab","AppleScript","OSC","MIDI/MSC"],"Intermediate",
"A QLab Cookbook workspace with script-cue generators for OSC, QLab-format OSC, MSC and MIDI program change cues. It saves hours of typing when QLab drives consoles or media servers.",
["Download the example workspace for your QLab version from the cookbook page.","Set up the template cue with the destination patch and message; for custom OSC put $$$ where the number should go (e.g. /track$$$/connect).","Run the generator's Script cue and answer the prompts for count, start value, increment and number format.","Copy the generated cues into your show workspace."],
[("Does it work in QLab 5?","Yes. It was written for QLab 3, and the page explains the QLab 4/5 changes (OSC cues became Network cues) and provides QLab 5 downloads."),("Where does AI fit?","An agent can draft the template values and counts from your paperwork, while the tested generator script creates the actual cues.")],"QLab Cookbook (Figure 53)")
n("Show Control","Batch-build QLab 5 cues from a spreadsheet export","https://www.taylorglad.com/post/qlab-5-batch-cue-generator-tsv-csv",["QLab 5","Google Sheets","AppleScript"],"Intermediate",
"Taylor Glad's script reads TSV/CSV exports from a Google Sheet template and creates 17 kinds of QLab cues in one pass. A spreadsheet produced by an AI or by paperwork tools becomes a cue list.",
["Copy the version 3 Google Sheet template linked in the post and fill in the tab for the cue type you need.","Export that tab as TSV (the post notes CSV can break on commas or quotes).","Paste the script into a Script cue, create any required network patch first, then run it and pick the files.","Trigger the script cue from a hotkey or Bitfocus Companion, as the author suggests."],
[("Why must patches exist first?","Network cues created before the patch is set up don't fix themselves later, so the script stops if the patch is missing."),("Can I import several files at once?","Yes. You can select multiple files of different types in one run.")],"Blog post by Taylor Glad")
n("Show Control","Automate show events with Bitfocus Companion triggers","https://companion.free/user-guide/v4.1/config/triggers/",["Bitfocus Companion"],"Beginner",
"Companion triggers run any button action automatically when an event happens, such as a time interval, a variable change or startup. They're the simplest automation layer to put under an agent.",
["Open the Triggers tab and click Add Trigger (new triggers start disabled).","Add Events such as Time interval or On variable change; any one event fires the trigger.","Add a Condition to filter, e.g. only when a variable equals 1.","Add Actions (anything a button can do, including pressing another button) and enable it."],
[("Are multiple events AND or OR?","OR: any event runs the trigger. Put AND logic in the Condition."),("How does this help AI workflows?","An agent can set a Companion variable or press a button, and tested triggers handle the rest.")],"Bitfocus Companion user guide")
n("Show Control","Send and receive arbitrary OSC from Companion buttons","https://bitfocus.io/connections/generic-osc",["Bitfocus Companion","OSC"],"Beginner",
"Companion's Generic OSC connection sends integers, floats, strings, blobs and multi-argument messages to any OSC device, and exposes received messages as variables.",
["Add an OSC Generic connection and set the target IP and port.","Put Send actions on buttons with the OSC path and value.","Turn on listening to capture incoming messages into variables like $(osc:latest_received_path).","Use those variables in triggers so devices or agents that speak OSC can drive Companion."],
[("Is the boolean type standard?","No. The module notes boolean isn't part of the OSC standard and may only work with some receivers."),("Can I read arguments?","Yes, with expressions like $(osc:latest_received_args)[0].")],"Bitfocus connection docs")
n("Show Control","Chase SMPTE, MTC and Art-Net timecode in Companion with TimeCore","https://bitfocus.io/connections/visualproductions-timecore",["Bitfocus Companion","Visual Productions TimeCore","Timecode"],"Intermediate",
"The TimeCore module brings a Visual Productions TimeCore into Companion, so buttons and triggers can show and react to incoming timecode.",
["Add the Visual Productions TimeCore connection in Companion and point it at the device.","Show variables such as $(…:tc_smpte) or tc_mtc on buttons for a timecode readout.","Use the Receiving feedbacks to flag when the timecode source drops.","Use actions to start, stop or set internal timecode and timers."],
[("Which sources are reported?","SMPTE/LTC, MTC, Art-Net, RTP-MIDI, sACN, TCP and UDP."),("Does it need hardware?","Yes, a TimeCore device.")],"Bitfocus connection docs")
n("Show Control","Expose Stream Deck actions to AI assistants with Elgato's MCP server","https://www.elgato.com/us/en/explorer/products/stream-deck/sd-mcp-setup/",["Elgato Stream Deck 7.4+","MCP","Claude Desktop"],"Beginner",
"Stream Deck 7.4 adds MCP support. Actions you put on a dedicated MCP Actions profile become tools that Claude Desktop or other AI clients can trigger.",
["In Stream Deck go to Preferences → General and enable MCP Deck. This creates the MCP Actions profile.","Drag only the actions you want the AI to reach onto that profile, and give each one a description.","Install Node.js, then add `npx --yes @elgato/mcp-server@latest` under mcpServers in claude_desktop_config.json.","Fully quit and reopen Claude, then check Settings → Developer shows elgato running."],
[("Can the AI see all my profiles?","No. Only actions on the MCP Actions profile are exposed."),("Does it work over HTTP?","Yes. `npx -y @elgato/mcp-server@latest --http` serves it on a local port for tools like G-Assist.")],"Elgato vendor guide")
n("Show Control","Trigger Stream Deck actions by voice with NVIDIA G-Assist","https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=VoY9XBpZuWA",["Elgato Stream Deck","NVIDIA Project G-Assist","MCP"],"Beginner",
"Elgato's video shows NVIDIA's Project G-Assist using voice to fire Stream Deck actions through the Stream Deck MCP server. This makes hands-free cueing possible for simple setups.",
["Enable MCP Deck in Stream Deck 7.4+ and put the allowed actions on the MCP Actions profile.","Install the Elgato MCP server globally (`npm install -g @elgato/mcp-server`) and run it, since G-Assist connects over the network.","Set up G-Assist per Elgato's guide and test with a harmless action first."],
[("Is voice control safe for a live show?","Keep it to non-critical actions. A misheard command shouldn't be able to fire a cue."),("Does it need an NVIDIA GPU?","G-Assist is NVIDIA's assistant. Check its requirements before planning around it.")],"Elgato on YouTube")
n("Show Control","Import timecode cue lists into ETC Eos over OSC","https://rsmck.co.uk/blog/eos-osc-timecode-companion/",["ETC Eos","CuePoints","OSC","Timecode"],"Intermediate",
"rsmck's EOS Timecode Companion takes a CuePoints export or any tab-delimited CSV and writes the timecode events into an Eos show over OSC, with no USB sticks.",
["Export your timecode cue points as a tab-delimited CSV (the post says not to use the Eos export option).","Run the cross-platform Electron app and point it at ETCnomad or a networked console.","Import the events, then review the timecode list on the desk."],
[("Does it work with CuePoints 2.0?","This version is kept for CSV and CuePoints 2.0 workflows. A separate CuePoints-1.x version is linked from the post."),("Multiple timecodes per cue?","Not supported at the time of the post.")],"Blog post by rsmck")
n("Show Control","Use AI as a show director behind safe TouchDesigner mappings","https://forum.derivative.ca/t/ai-controlled-parties-with-touchdesigner-tdmcp-concept-feedback-welcome/993426",["TouchDesigner","tdmcp","LLM"],"Advanced",
"A Derivative forum thread proposing an AI layer that picks pre-approved cues and moods. Hazardous effects stay operator-only, and changes go through dry runs and approval queues.",
["Define a list of pre-approved cues and moods in TouchDesigner; this is all the AI may request.","Route AI output through a policy step: show intent, then a policy decision, then an approval queue or dry run.","Keep lasers, moving heads, blackout, PA and audio routing blocked or operator-only.","Rehearse with a simulated DMX output before connecting any real fixtures."],
[("Is this a finished product?","No. It's a concept thread, and the related tdmcp docs call the implementation a rehearsal proof of concept."),("Who is it for?","Small clubs and parties without a pre-produced show, where an operator wants help adapting visuals live.")],"Derivative forum")
n("Production Ops","Extract mic cues from a script with ChatGPT and convert them for an X32","https://www.reddit.com/r/livesound/comments/1omznva/how_or_with_what_have_you_implemented_artificial/",["ChatGPT Deep Research","Python","Behringer X32"],"Intermediate",
"An r/livesound user describes having ChatGPT Deep Research pull sound and lighting cues and character entrances and exits from a script, cross-reference them to mic channels, and output a spreadsheet that a Python script turned into X32 snippets.",
["Give the model the script and your mic-to-character channel list.","Ask for a spreadsheet of mic cues (cue, character, channel, on/off) and check it against the script.","Use a small script to turn the sheet into X32 scene or snippet data.","Load the result on a test console and compare it with your own mute plan."],
[("Did it work?","The poster said the proof of concept worked, but they still did the mutes by hand for the show."),("What's the risk?","Missed or invented cues, so treat the output as a draft to check.")],"Reddit r/livesound")
n("Production Ops","Draft stage plots and input lists from a text description or photo","https://www.reddit.com/r/livesound/comments/1n3x68u/a_modern_web_app_for_stage_plots_and_input_lists/",["Stage plot app","AI"],"Beginner",
"An r/livesound thread about a web app that creates a starting stage plot from a short description or a photo, with a linked input list. Engineers in the thread push back on how reliable AI is for this.",
["Describe the act (e.g. \"4-piece rock band with keys\") or upload an existing plot or photo.","Let the tool create the plot and linked input list, then fix positions and channels by hand.","Export and share with the band and house crew, then confirm the details with the artist."],
[("Do engineers trust it?","Opinions are mixed. Some say a simple wizard beats AI, and collaboration features got the most interest."),("Best use?","As a fast first draft before a proper advance.")],"Reddit r/livesound")
n("Production Ops","Run one live production schedule with AI conflict checks","https://showops.ai/produce",["ShowOps.AI"],"Beginner",
"ShowOps.AI's Produce module keeps a single schedule across departments from load-in to strike. It flags conflicts such as overlapping dock use and creates call sheets once staffing is confirmed.",
["Load departments, spaces and load-in-to-strike tasks into Produce.","Connect venue readiness and staffing rosters so schedule constraints and call sheets follow them.","Review flagged conflicts (e.g. AV lift and catering sharing a dock) and resolve them."],
[("Is it free?","It's a commercial product. Check the vendor for pricing."),("What does the AI do?","According to the vendor, it cross-references departments, spaces and time to find conflicts.")],"ShowOps.AI vendor page")
n("Production Ops","Keep lighting paperwork in sync with an Eos console","https://lightassistant.com/",["Light Assistant","ETC Eos","Vectorworks","OSC"],"Beginner",
"Light Assistant builds cue sheets, spot sheets, hookups and schedules. During tech it follows Eos consoles over OSC so notes stay attached to the right cue.",
["Build the cue sheet as a storyboard, then sync labels, scene breaks and page numbers to Eos.","Exchange instrument data with Vectorworks when you choose to sync.","During tech let it follow Eos over OSC and take notes that link to cues and fixtures.","Export PDFs (cue sheets, hookups, color cuts) for the crew."],
[("Is there a free tier?","Yes. There's a limited free version and a web app, alongside subscription and perpetual plans."),("Is it AI?","It's automation, not an LLM, but it's a solid data source for agent-written paperwork.")],"Light Assistant vendor site")
n("Production Ops","Mark up scripts and export cue lists straight to Eos with Promptbook","https://applebytechnical.com/promptbook",["Promptbook","ETC Eos","QLab"],"Beginner",
"Promptbook is a digital prompt book for stage managers. It handles script markup, automatic standbys, live Eos and QLab cue tracking, and CSV export for import into ETC Eos.",
["Import the script PDF or Word document and create colour-coded cue lists.","Drag across a line to place a cue; standbys are generated automatically from GO cues.","Export a PDF prompt book, a cue sheet spreadsheet or an Eos CSV.","In show mode, connect to auto-discovered Eos and QLab machines to track cues live."],
[("What happens when the script changes?","Upload the revised script and it moves cues across, suggesting matches or asking you to review where lines changed."),("Cost?","Core features are free, and Pro adds QLab/Eos tracking and more.")],"Appleby Technical vendor page")
n("TouchDesigner","Add ChatGPT and Whisper speech-to-text components to TouchDesigner","https://derivative.ca/community-post/tutorial/custom-chatgpt-and-whisperspeech-text-plugins-touchdesigner/67446",["TouchDesigner","OpenAI Whisper","ChatGPT"],"Beginner",
"A Derivative community tutorial by blankensmithing on two components that run Whisper speech-to-text and ChatGPT inside TouchDesigner with only an OpenAI API key.",
["Get the project file and components linked in the tutorial (hosted on the author's Patreon).","Add your OpenAI API key to the components.","Wire Whisper's transcript into ChatGPT, or into text and visual parameters, to build voice-reactive installations."],
[("Is it free?","The tutorial is free. The components are linked via the author's Patreon, and API usage is billed by OpenAI."),("Is it local?","No. It calls OpenAI's hosted APIs.")],"Derivative community tutorial")
for cat,title,url,tools,diff,summ,steps,faqs,label in N:
    slug=re.sub(r'[^a-z0-9]+','-',title.lower()).strip('-')[:70].strip('-')
    q=lambda s:'"'+s.replace('"','\\"')+'"'
    fm=f"---\ntitle: {q(title)}\nslug: {slug}\ncategory: {q(cat)}\ntools: [{', '.join(q(t) for t in tools)}]\ndifficulty: {diff}\nsource_url: {url}\nsummary: {q(summ)}\n---\n"
    b=f"\n## What it does\n\n{summ}\n\n## How to set it up\n\n"+"\n".join(f"{i+1}. {s}" for i,s in enumerate(steps))+f"\n\nSource: [{label}]({url})\n\n## FAQ\n\n"+"\n\n".join(f"### {a}\n{b_}" for a,b_ in faqs)+"\n"
    p=f"content/use-cases/{slug}.md"; assert not os.path.exists(p),p
    open(p,'w').write(fm+b)
print(len(N))
